        <exercise id="e34dd45b-d934-43e2-a0c2-00692e36905a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00016">
            <para id="para-00142">Are the solutions and the graph for the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> similar?</para>
            <para id="para-00143">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00144">They are similar because the solutions are close</para>
            <para id="para-00145">They are not similar because the square root of a number is always positive.</para>
            <para id="para-00146">They are not similar.</para>
            <para id="para-00147">They are similar because the square root of a number is always positive.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00016">
            <para id="para-00148">Correct! They are similar because the solutions are close. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.873</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mn>5.873</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00149">Try again. Revisit activities 9.5.3 and 9.5.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00150">The correct answer is:They are similar because the solutions are close. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1.873</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msqrt><m:mrow><m:mn>15</m:mn></m:mrow></m:msqrt><m:mo>≈</m:mo><m:mn>5.873</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. You seem to be struck. Who can you ask for help?</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
